 "_doc": "Odysseus (GAME_DESIGN.md: Heroes; art 10/31/2026). Built by tools/art/build_odysseus.py on the shared body in tools/art/hero_kit.py; rules in docs/ART_RULES.md. The pilos, the pointed felt cap of a sailor and traveller, is how Greek vase painting and sculpture mark Odysseus; a dark beard (Odyssey 16.176). From Odyssey 19.225-232, the clothes he wore to Troy: a purple woollen cloak fastened with a gold brooch, and a shining tunic, shown here as a purple tunic to the knees with a gold brooch at the shoulder. A belt and sandals. Mediterranean skin. His great bow (Odyssey 21) is drawn separately (data/art/weapons/) at his hand.",
